        items: [
          '**Fewer seats sold per vehicle** — photographers need a row each (or the whole vehicle); empty seats are the honest cost of elbow room and clean angles.',
          '**Prime-location camps** — sleeping inside the productive zones (Ndutu in February, the north in August) costs more and saves the golden hour from being spent in transit.',
          '**Longer duration** — portfolios are built on repetition and luck-surface-area. Ten days materially outperforms seven; we will always advocate for the extra days over the fancier lodge.',
          '**Private vehicle upgrades** — the full-vehicle option removes every compromise and is the standard choice for serious shooters and small photo groups.',
        ],
